---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const rows=core.orders.map(o=>({id:o.order_id,p:core.payments.find(p=>p.order_id===o.order_id&&p.method==='card')}));
---
<figure class="outer-figure" data-outer-filter aria-labelledby="r05-outer-title">
 <figcaption id="r05-outer-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Where does the card condition act?</figcaption>
 <div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Placement of the card condition"><button type="button" data-mode="on" aria-pressed="true">In ON</button><button type="button" data-mode="where" aria-pressed="false">In WHERE</button></div>
 <p class="condition" data-condition>ON p.order_id = o.order_id AND p.method = 'card'</p>
 <table><caption>Orders after the left join and filter</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Order</th><th scope="col">Payment</th><th scope="col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(r=><tr data-unmatched={!r.p?'yes':'no'}><th scope="row">{r.id}</th><td>{r.p?r.p.payment_id:<em>NULL</em>}</td><td>{r.p?r.p.amount:<em>NULL</em>}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
 <p data-explanation aria-live="polite">Order 103 has no card match. The left join preserves it, with missing payment columns.</p>
 <details><summary>Both answers as text</summary><p>With the condition in ON, orders 101, 102 and 103 remain; their card payments are 501, 503 and no match. With the condition in WHERE, only 101 and 102 remain. The generated missing payment method on 103 does not equal 'card'.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-outer-filter]').forEach(root=>root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-mode]').forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
 const on=button.dataset.mode==='on';root.querySelectorAll('[data-mode]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-unmatched="yes"]').forEach(r=>r.hidden=!on);
 root.querySelector('[data-condition]')!.textContent=on?"ON p.order_id = o.order_id AND p.method = 'card'":"ON p.order_id = o.order_id · WHERE p.method = 'card'";
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=on?'Order 103 has no card match. The left join preserves it, with missing payment columns.':'WHERE tests the joined rows. On order 103, the missing method makes the test unknown, so that row is discarded.';
 })));
</script>
<style>
.outer-figure{font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.92rem;margin:2.5rem 0;padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong)}figcaption{font-size:1.08rem;margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;margin-right:.6rem}.choices{display:flex;gap:.5rem}.choices button{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);padding:.6rem 1rem;border-radius:.25rem;cursor:pointer}.choices button[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--color-accent);border-color:var(--color-accent);color:var(--color-surface)}button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}.condition{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.82rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere;min-height:3em}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{padding:.6rem;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong)}caption{text-align:left;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin:.6rem 0}[data-explanation]{border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.7rem;min-height:4.5em}details{font-size:.85rem}[hidden]{display:none}
</style>
